From 1a9ae21398dba8ba933b4c2e3feb2a4af4324d73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joey <joey@evolution-x.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:59:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: Add non-Pixel ambient Now Playing indicator, fall
 back to native on Pixel

Ports the visual and animation language of Google's Pixel ambient music
indication (collapsed pill, spring-animated song-change slide, expand-to-card
with album-art background and Monet-derived color scheme) into a new,
self-contained package, com.android.systemui.nowplaying.ambient, that has no
dependency on com.google.android.as or any com.google.android.ambientindication.*
broadcast. Unlike the real Pixel implementation, this fork is driven entirely
by NowPlayingViewController's existing MediaSessionManager data, so it works
on any device rather than only Pixels with AS installed.

NowPlayingAmbientContainer replaces the previous canvas-drawn NowPlayingView
as the primary now-playing surface. It supports track/artist text, app or
generic music-note icon styles, accent/album/white text coloring, adjustable
text sizes, lyrics (via the existing LyricsFetcher, with a lightweight update
path that bypasses the track-change slide animation so per-line lyric updates
don't trigger expensive transitions), and tap-to-expand into an album-art-
backed card when art is available. Favoriting and default-music-player launch
actions from the original Pixel implementation are intentionally not ported,
since MediaSessionManager has no equivalent data source for either.

The view is now anchored to the keyguard root ConstraintLayout via
NowPlayingKeyguardSection, registered under KEYGUARD_NOW_PLAYING_SECTION in
KeyguardSectionsModule and wired into DefaultKeyguardBlueprint's section list
alongside the other optional keyguard sections. This matches how Google's own
DefaultAmbientIndicationAreaSection positions the Pixel ambient indication: on
UDFPS devices, the view fills the space between device_entry_icon_view and
keyguard_indication_area; on non-UDFPS devices, its bottom edge sits above
device_entry_icon_view with a fixed margin, and no opposing top constraint is
applied, so the WRAP_CONTENT-height view resolves its position from that
single anchor rather than being centered across the full keyguard height. The
view is no longer managed by CentralSurfacesImpl or added to the custom
overlay container, which previously caused it to appear near the media player
instead of the lockscreen bottom area.

NowPlayingAmbientViewModel ports two behaviors from Google's
KeyguardAmbientIndicationViewModel and KeyguardAmbientIndicationAreaViewBinder
that the initial port omitted. First, AOD burn-in-protection translation:
the same BurnInInteractor offsets used elsewhere on the keyguard are applied
to the ambient pill via translationX/translationY, scaled by the AOD
transition factor, so the pill drifts in sync with other burn-in-protected
elements instead of sitting static in one spot for hours during doze. Second,
tap-outside-to-collapse: taps on the keyguard root view outside the pill's
own bounds now collapse an expanded album-art card, sourced from
KeyguardRootViewModel's existing lastRootViewTapPosition flow.
NowPlayingViewController collects both flows only while the ambient container
is attached, using repeatWhenAttached/repeatOnLifecycle to avoid leaking
collection when the view isn't in the hierarchy (e.g. on Pixel devices where
NowPlayingKeyguardSection never adds it).

PixelAmbientIndicationDetector gates this fork off on devices that are both
Pixel-branded hardware and have a running com.google.android.as install,
since those devices already have a functional native ambient indication path
and should not run a second, competing implementation. NowPlayingViewController
checks this at startup and, when true, skips all setup (media monitoring,
settings observation, burn-in/tap-outside observation, ScrimUtils
registration), leaving the real com.google.android.systemui.ambientmusic
stack to run independently and untouched. NowPlayingKeyguardSection similarly
no-ops on Pixel so no view is added to the keyguard layout on those devices.

Several polish items bring this fork closer to parity with Google's reference
implementation. Track/artist text views now ellipsize instead of hard-
clipping when content overflows, matching AmbientIndicationContainer's
updateTextEllipsizing() behavior. Tapping the collapsed pill to expand now
goes through FalsingManager.isFalseTap() and calls
PowerInteractor.wakeUpIfDozing() before expanding, mirroring Google's
onWrapperClick()/onTextClick() guards so accidental pocket/AOD touches don't
silently expand the card. The collapsed pill now sets a content description
("Now playing: <track> by <artist>") and toggles
isImportantForAccessibility, giving TalkBack users something to announce where
previously the container was unlabeled.

nowplaying_use_compact_style and nowplaying_vertical_position are dropped,
since neither has a natural home in the new fixed-anchor pill/card layout;
all other existing Now Playing settings (nowplaying_enabled, color mode, icon
style/size, text sizes, show-on-lockscreen/AOD, tap-to-expand, lyrics mode)
continue to apply to the new implementation. media_waveform_seekbar
(nowplaying_use_waveform_seekbar) is also removed from
NowPlayingSettingsRepository, since the settings screen never exposed a
control for it and the seek-bar UI that consumed it was removed along with
the old canvas-drawn NowPlayingView/NowPlayingExpandedOverlay.

